From: Tilo maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] octeontx2-af: only build CN20K debugfs with CONFIG_DEBUG_FS

The debugfs member of struct rvu and the CN20K debugfs caller in
rvu_debugfs.c are already guarded by CONFIG_DEBUG_FS. Building the new
CN20K debugfs implementation unconditionally fails with DEBUG_FS=n.
Keep the hardware driver enabled and select only its debugfs object
conditionally, matching the existing caller and data layout.

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/marvell/octeontx2/af/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/marvell/octeontx2/af/Makefile
@@ -12,5 +12,7 @@
 		  rvu_reg.o rvu_npc.o rvu_debugfs.o ptp.o rvu_npc_fs.o \
 		  rvu_cpt.o rvu_devlink.o rpm.o rvu_cn10k.o rvu_switch.o \
 		  rvu_sdp.o rvu_npc_hash.o mcs.o mcs_rvu_if.o mcs_cnf10kb.o \
-		  rvu_rep.o cn20k/mbox_init.o cn20k/nix.o cn20k/debugfs.o \
+		  rvu_rep.o cn20k/mbox_init.o cn20k/nix.o \
 		  cn20k/npa.o cn20k/npc.o
+
+rvu_af-$(CONFIG_DEBUG_FS) += cn20k/debugfs.o
